#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ExifTool print format for the sensor data in a GoPro video.
# Used by sensors.py. ExifTool prints the first three lines below once for
# every block of sensor data in the file (the camera stores one block per
# second):
#
#   T|<start of the block in seconds>|<length of the block in seconds>
#   A|<accelerometer values, three numbers per measurement>
#   G|<gyroscope values, three numbers per measurement>
#
# and the last line once for every GPS point (10 per second):
#
#   S|<speed in km/h>|<fix: 0 = no satellites found, 2 or 3 = position known>
#
# A line is left out when the file has no such data.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#[BODY]T|$SampleTime|$SampleDuration
#[BODY]A|$Accelerometer
#[BODY]G|$Gyroscope
#[BODY]S|$GPSSpeed|$GPSMeasureMode
